-> Purchase Order (PO) & Vendor Management Module
Why it matters: Right now, your inventory can be audited, but you lack an end-to-end workflow to restock items when they run low.
What it entails:
A vendor directory (VendorModel) to store supplier contact info and lead times.
A PurchaseOrderFormScreen where managers/admins can order stock variants from specific vendors.
A Goods Received Note (GRN) or receiving workflow (ReceiveGoodsScreen) that automatically updates your variant stock quantities once a supplier shipment arrives at the warehouse.

-> Immutable Stock Ledger (StockLedgerScreen)
Why it matters: In an enterprise ERP, you need complete visibility and traceability into why inventory levels changed (e.g., sold via POS, adjusted via stock audit, or received via purchase order).
What it entails:
A searchable log collection (stock_movements) that automatically records every transaction (timestamp, SKU, quantity change, user ID, reference ID like Order ID or Audit ID, and movement type: SALE, RESTOCK, ADJUSTMENT, RETURN).

-> Dedicated POS Checkout & Payment Screen
Why it matters: If your system is used in a physical retail environment, cashiers need a fast, distraction-free checkout experience separate from standard backend order creation.
What it entails:
A grid-based quick-select product grid.
A shopping cart drawer supporting barcode scanning, manual discounts, tax calculations, and split payment methods (Cash, Card, Store Credit).
Instant generation of printable or digital invoices/receipts.